#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
Attendance Tracker - Excel workbook generator
=============================================
Creates  Attendance_Tracker.xlsx  (plain .xlsx, no macros) with these tabs:

  Dashboard        Yellow filters: Year / Month / Team / Sub Team
                     - KPI cards: headcount, present, leave, absent, unmarked, block leave
                     - Team-wise & Sub-team-wise: present, leave, absent, block leave used/balance
                     - Month-wise trend table + chart
                     - Employee-wise: present, leave, absent, block leave used/balance,
                       PL / SL / WFH / NCRW / WFO utilized & balance
  Employee Master  200 slots: ID, name, team, sub team, employment type, manager,
                   block leave status, block leave date (+ optional opening PL carry-forward)
  Leave Codes      Your code table + Category / Balance Limit settings that drive the dashboard
  Holidays         Holiday calendar (add next year's holidays in the empty rows)
  Jan-2026 ...     One attendance tab per month - dropdown codes, colour coded
  Calc, Data       Hidden helper sheets that feed the dashboard - don't edit

Run
  python build_attendance_tracker.py               -> blank tracker
  python build_attendance_tracker.py --sample      -> filled with dummy data to preview the dashboard
  python build_attendance_tracker.py --out X.xlsx  -> custom file name
Needs: openpyxl   (pip install openpyxl)
"""

